 # llama.cpp measured against the Python mlx-lm baseline
 
+> **Revision-2 instrumentation, 2026-08-30:** no benchmark rerun was performed
+> in this revision. The next run must use the merged 76,800-token live KV bound,
+> timestamped 20 Hz physical-footprint observations with bounded 0.2 Hz `vmmap`,
+> synchronous window-boundary samples, and MTP observed off. A scored window
+> additionally proves every successful timestamp gap is at most 125 ms; sparse,
+> untimestamped, failed, partial, or malformed series are refused. The
+> provisional numbers below remain historical and are not a decision set.
+>
+> Both cache-policy asymmetries must be presented together in that run:
+>
+> - Python-only `--prompt-cache-size 1 --prompt-cache-bytes 8GB` can reduce TTFT
+>   on a repeated prompt and can retain up to the configured cache budget;
+>   direction for a cold, unique prompt is unknown.
+> - llama.cpp per-slot KV reuse can reduce TTFT when a slot reuses a matching
+>   prefix and can retain slot-local KV state; direction without an observed
+>   reuse hit is unknown.
+>
+> Any scenario where either policy produced an observed reuse hit while the
+> other did not is non-comparable and must be refused rather than scored.
+
 Task: TASK-260828-2wcrph (story STORY-260828-2faxgm)
 Date: 2026-08-29
 Author role: developer
